{"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"tokens":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"partSymbol","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLPartSymbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPartSymbol","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL13MXLPartSymbolV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"discussion","type":"heading","text":"Discussion","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Maps to a nested MusicXML ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"<part-symbol>"},{"text":" element.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLAttributes\/partSymbol","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"kind":"symbol","variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlattributes\/partsymbol"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLAttributes"]]},"sections":[],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The part-symbol element indicates how a symbol for a multi-staff part is indicated in the score."}],"metadata":{"symbolKind":"property","externalID":"s:7IvorMXL13MXLAttributesV10partSymbolAA07MXLPartE0VSgvp","modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"roleHeading":"Instance Property","role":"symbol","title":"partSymbol","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"partSymbol","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLPartSymbol","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL13MXLPartSymbolV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}]},"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLAttributes/partSymbol":{"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlattributes\/partsymbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLAttributes\/partSymbol","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The part-symbol element indicates how a symbol for a multi-staff part is indicated in the score."}],"title":"partSymbol","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"partSymbol","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLPartSymbol","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL13MXLPartSymbolV"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLAttributes":{"type":"topic","title":"MXLAttributes","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLAttributes","abstract":[{"text":"The attributes element contains musical information that typically changes on measure boundaries. This","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"includes key and time signatures, clefs, transpositions, and staving. When attributes are changed mid-measure,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it affects the music in score order, not in MusicXML document order.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLAttributes"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLAttributes"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlattributes"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"type":"topic","title":"IvorMXL","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}],"role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLPartSymbol":{"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPartSymbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLPartSymbol","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlpartsymbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLPartSymbol","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"MXLPartSymbol","abstract":[{"text":"The part-symbol type indicates how a symbol for a multi-staff part is indicated in the score; brace is the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"default value. The top-staff and bottom-staff attributes are used when the brace does not extend across the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"entire part. For example, in a 3-staff organ part, the top-staff will typically be 1 for the right hand, while","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the bottom-staff will typically be 2 for the left hand. Staff 3 for the pedals is usually outside the brace.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"By default, the presence of a part-symbol element that does not extend across the entire part also indicates a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"corresponding change in the common barlines within a part.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic"}}}